# trace-quirks.ti59 Q quirk that enables some sort of trace mode on the printer.
# From Magatzine "TI PPC NOTES", V6N4-5P17, 1981
#
# Note that the article has a typo: What is shown on the display is "7993", not "9993".
#
# These are the original notes in the article:
#
# QUIRK- John Miranda (the youngest member, I suppose, at 14) found this quirk in the
# TI-58. I tested it and found it to work in the TI-59 as well. With the printer attached,
# it puts the calculator in TRACE mode. RST kills this state.
#
# From turn-on press:
# CP LRN LBL A FIX O R/S LRN 999 + . 00000999 = A STF IND 7 INV LRN
#
# The display nows says 9993 00. You can SST through it to 99999 when it reverts to
# step 000 and you see your program LBL A FIX 0 R/S again.
#
# If you BST, you loose the display, but stay with the TRACE mode. But it is impossible
# to go back into LRN at this point, unless you press GTO 000 then LRN.
# The "listing" of your program you now get, if you press SST repeatedly, is SR-52-like,
# no mnemonics, just the program step and the key code.
#
# Further investigating invited from the membership.

MODEL: TI-58
PRINTER: on

# Prepare the magnet card inlay
CUECARD:
Template: MagnetCard
Title: Trace Quirk
Banks: 1
Row1: From Magatzine "TI PPC NOTES", V6N4-5P17, 1981
Row1Align: center

PROGRAM:
000  76 LBL
001  11  A
002  58 FIX
003  00  00
004  91 R/S


# Brings the display to the described state:
KEYSTROKES:
64 9
64 9
64 9
85 +
93 ,
92 0
92 0
92 0
92 0
92 0
64 9
64 9
64 9
95 =
11 A
21 2nd
81 St flg
21 2nd
45 Ind
62 7
22 INV
31 LRN